CHANGED FC1-c009 L01 T d/(1 − φ(1 − ρ)), where φ, with 0 ≤ φ ≤ 1, is the share of each loan redeposited at the bank. The rest is held as cash outside the bank. This needs A1 with 0 < ρ ≤ 1, and the no-withdrawal and no-repayment parts of A3 (Proposition 3.5).
CHANGED FC1-c064 L04 None An incoming order meets the best price on the opposite side first. Among resting orders at that price it meets the earliest arrival first (Definition 2.1).
CHANGED FC1-c101 L05 T Under A1, each buyer and seller of a trade differ and its quantity and price are positive integers. Then 0 ≤ NP ≤ G, so net payments are non-negative and at most gross payments, where G is the sum of the considerations (Proposition 2.1(ii)).
CHANGED FC1-c150 L02 None A claim with terms, as the opening paragraph of the lesson states it.
CHANGED FC1-c152 L01 T Yes. Under A2′ with 0 ≤ φ ≤ 1, A1 with 0 < ρ ≤ 1 and the no-withdrawal and no-repayment parts of A3, d/(1 − φ(1 − ρ)) is at most d/ρ, with equality if and only if φ = 1 or ρ = 1 (Proposition 3.5).
